    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 449,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Optimal therapy for reduction of lipoprotein(a).\nThese may both lower Lp(a) and cardiovascular risk of the patients. Besides inhibiting platelet function, antiplatelet therapy with aspirin may also decrease the plasma concentration of Lp(a) and modulate its influence on platelets. WHAT IS NEW AND CONCLUSION We highlight the inadequacy of current approaches for lowering Lp(a) and draw attention to novel insights that may lead to better treatment."
